---
![](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f926f7fd-e7be-4faf-aa38-06ac40da4938)


{{% steps %}}

### Step 1
Support yourself on the parallel bars with your arms straight. Inhale and slowly lower your body by bending your elbows to about a 90-degree angle.

### Step 2
Lower yourself as far as your strength and shoulder flexibility comfortably allow. Exhale and press through your hands to push yourself back up to the starting position.

{{% /steps %}}

{{< callout type="info" >}}
• Aim to lower down until your upper arms are roughly parallel to the floor (elbows bent at 90 degrees).

• To target the chest more, lean your torso slightly forward and allow your elbows to flare out slightly. However, avoid going too wide or too deep if it causes discomfort in your shoulders.
{{< /callout >}}
